E. Proof interpretation
  The harmonic/Mertens budget is useful as an owner-debt priority queue:
    small budget = far-tail endpoint owners, often E-only spine debt;
    large budget = low-owner mixed walls, often the true obstruction boundary.
  But the scalar budget collides across branch masks and wall signatures.
  Therefore an Euler-Mascheroni-style tail normalizer can only be a sidecar
  attached to HYP-3427/HYP-3429 endpoint windows, not a floor certificate.

